<!-- [GREEDY WINDOW 2026-11-10] Greedy (wolffloatergreedy.cpp; ticket 721; region-terrain-work/greedy-dice-2026-11-10/README.md).
     Paul: "anything we make like that must be built into the viewer NOT a hud", "the UI for Greedy should SCALE with the
     user's UI settings" (a floater does: UI Size and the font settings apply), "so the greedy is up to the user".
     Who and why: a resident aged 35-65 wants a friendly game of dice with friends, here or anywhere on the grid. They open
     Wolf World > Greedy, start or join a game, and press ROLL / BANK in big buttons.
     Three views, chosen with the View buttons at the top and remembered (WolfGreedyMode):
       FULL  - the whole game: whose turn, the players and their scores, this turn, the dice, ROLL / BANK, the game buttons
       TABLE - controls only, for when a Greedy table in-world is the big display: whose turn, your score, ROLL / BANK
       STRIP - a small bar at the bottom of the screen, to keep playing while walking, flying or sailing
     Sitting at a Greedy table OFFERS the table view (the offer bar), never forces it. The guide (HOW TO PLAY) shows in the
     full view. Messages and errors stay in the message line until the next action (never a countdown, never a flash). -->
